      "later_exact_user_messages": [
        {"source_ordinal":13748,"user_text_utf8":"ok so the goal isnt complete.  you need to make sure the cursor, codex, and qwen models pass too.  Do two passes on them.\n","user_text_utf8_bytes":122,"user_text_sha256":"5715c13d462b22afa481b8ae7d0764b540bf5192664861911e70a47f92b48788"},
        {"source_ordinal":14829,"user_text_utf8":"Have you tried taking going through the whole automated system(stopping before work node creation) and seeing if your solution works?  You wouldn't process all of the plans, but pick one of the larger plan docs to do as a test.  This would be sandboxed.  The have all of the 12 models run through it twice.  Start with ox-alpha-free, max and cursor/default, effort auto.\n","user_text_utf8_bytes":371,"user_text_sha256":"5cb4e366adf20ec27742c0a6e4fc419332eeab9f30c8de5c93405f13829729de"},
        {"source_ordinal":23490,"user_text_utf8":"Complete the bounded-context PuppetMaster architecture qualification using the already-completed Storage Plan as a sandboxed end-to-end pre-WorkNode test: preserve canonical Plans and ledger unchanged; compile only bounded task-specific PromptCapsules; empirically qualify the exact 12 prescribed routes twice on unchanged bytes/configuration, using native OMP /goal with both advisor controls off for OMP routes and native Codex App Goal with one ordinary prompt beginning 'Create a goal that' for Codex routes; require exact typed output, native Goal activation and terminal evidence, unique fresh row identity, deterministic host validation, no WorkNode creation, no retries or retro-credit, and preserve all failures. Use Ox max first, Cursor auto second, Qwen last, and do not spend paid/Codex/Cursor tokens until the free Ox harness passes cleanly.","user_text_utf8_bytes":854,"user_text_sha256":"c532a6447d45d9d2d0200281010b5e989fbe12f108d27eb913d60b772fb16ca6"}
      ],
